===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nl|dum|vri}}, from {{inh|nl|odt|frī}}, from {{inh|nl|gmw-pro|*frī}}, from {{inh|nl|gem-pro|*frijaz}}, from {{inh|nl|ine-pro|*priHyós}}, a derivation from {{m|ine-pro|*preyH-||to be fond of}}. Related to {{m|nl|vrijen||to make love}}, {{m|nl|vrijdag||Friday}}, {{m|nl|vriend||friend}}, and {{m|nl|vrede||peace}}.

====Adjective====
{{nl-adj}}

# [[free]]; not [[imprisoned]] or [[enslaved]].
#: {{syn|nl|op vrije voet}}
#: {{ant|nl|onvrij}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik ben geen nummer, ik ben een '''vrij''' [[man]]!|I am not a number, I am a '''free''' man!|inline=1}}
# [[free]]; unconstrained.
#: {{syn|nl|onbelemmerd|ongehinderd}}
#: {{ant|nl|belemmerd|gehinderd}} 
#: {{uxi|nl|Hij had de '''vrije''' [[hand]] over het [[land]].|He had a '''free''' hand over the land.|inline=1}}
# [[free]]; unobstructed, without [[blockage|blockages]].
#: {{uxi|nl|De [[afvoer]] was '''vrij'''.|The drain was '''clear'''.|inline=1}}
# [[free]]; without [[obligation]]s or [[work]].
#: {{uxi|nl|[[vrije tijd|'''vrije''' tijd]]|'''free''' time|inline=1}}
#: {{uxi|nl|Ik heb twee dagen '''vrij''' gevraagd aan mijn baas.|I asked my boss for two days '''off'''.}}

